</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/coa/coa/en/item/16265/index.do?q=%222014+ONCA+194%22">Winters v. Hunking</a></span>
                        - <span class="citation">2017 ONCA 909</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2017-11-27</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Civil</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    As this Court has stated, in the context of setting aside default judgments generally, the various applicable factors are not to be treated as rigid rules; the ultimate task on such a motion is “to determine whether the interests of justice favour granting the order”: Mountain View Farms Ltd. v. McQueen, <b>2014 ONCA 194</b>, 317 
                </p>
